  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "high",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Manual validation only; scripts were not runnable in this environment. Present maximum inherent risk is critical from the untrusted ticket_message to service-role SQL read plus customer-visible writeback path. Residual falls one tier to high because the only declared control on that path is a high-volume raw-action approval gate, which earns one tier of step-2 credit and cannot sever or constrain the sink. Forecast returns to critical if autonomy increases or the approval gate is removed; the control whose decay moves the forecast most is ctl.tool_call_prompt. A separate present high finding exists for the unpinned, identity-unverified Supabase MCP server."
  },
